          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बळद (baḷad) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from balivarda, \"ox, bull\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry (CDIAL 9176); the match is through Gujarati baḷad and Hindi balad. CDIAL records a view that the Sanskrit word joins balin, \"strong\", with a non-Aryan word for \"ox\"."
            }
          ]
        },
